From: Daniel Özdek <daniel.timur.23@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Read the cursor position through Quartz instead of the main thread

NtUserGetCursorPos asks the driver whenever the mouse has been still for
100 ms. The driver dispatched to the Cocoa main thread for every call
(~12 us, longer while the main thread presents frames). CGEventCreate(NULL)
returns the same Quartz coordinates on any thread (~0.1 us).
Measured with a GetCursorPos loop: 10.8-12.1 us -> 0.46-0.96 us per call.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -2829,6 +2829,19 @@
  */
 int macdrv_get_cursor_position(CGPoint *pos)
 {
+    /* Quartz reports the global cursor location (already in the flipped, top-left
+       origin that flippedMouseLocation produces) and is thread-safe. GetCursorPos
+       lands here whenever the mouse has been still for 100 ms, and games poll it
+       every frame: a round trip to the main thread costs ~12 us and also waits
+       behind whatever the main thread is doing (presenting, window events). */
+    CGEventRef event = CGEventCreate(NULL);
+    if (event)
+    {
+        *pos = cgpoint_win_from_mac(CGEventGetLocation(event));
+        CFRelease(event);
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+
     OnMainThread(^{
         NSPoint location = [NSEvent mouseLocation];
         location = [[WineApplicationController sharedController] flippedMouseLocation:location];
